%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%% 
I'm leaving my comments here: 
Wearing lipstick: rank correlations ~0.97-1.0 --> lrp distributes
same ranking signal to every subspace w/ different scaling. i.e., group means
vary in magnitude but ordering of examples is the same, hence identical 
AP everywhere. Maybe lipstick and gender is too confounded.
 
Blond Hair: somewhat decorrelated: sub 4,3 = 0.643, sub 4,6 = 0.653, sub 4,0 = 0.684
sub 6,12: highest gender signal
sub 4: Low gender AP, AttrAP=0.901

Summary: 
wearing lipstick subspaces are useless
blond hair subspaces are not great, but we could try:
remove 6,12,10 from sx16. The most promising candidate to keep 
based on raw stats is sub 4 (one of the 'eyes' subspaces),
w/ lowest genderAP (0.763) and decorrelated from gender heavy subs

